@startuml
' Opportunistic DTLS of an RPC connection - see the STARTDTLS description in
' service-rpc/service/esdm_rpc_protocol.h and common/esdm_dtls.h
skinparam defaultFontName "Liberation Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #000000
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #000000
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEEEEE
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #000000
hide footbox

participant "RPC client\n(libesdm_rpc_client)" as C
participant "esdm-server" as S

note over C, S: SOCK_SEQPACKET connection, in the clear
C -> S: STARTDTLS request\n(method index 0x534c5444 "DTLS", no message)
C -> S: probe request without waiting\n(GetPoolsize / RndAddEntropy without data)
alt server with DTLS
  S --> C: SUCCESS, message "DTLS"
  S --> C: answer to the probe
  C <-> S: DTLS 1.2 handshake\n(ephemeral ECDH, AEAD, self-signed\nserver certificate not verified)
  C -> S: request in DTLS records\n(one record per socket message)
  S --> C: answer in DTLS records
else server without DTLS, or --no_dtls
  S --> C: SERVICE_FAILED
  S --> C: answer to the probe
  C -> S: request in the clear
  S --> C: answer in the clear
else server 1.2.3 and before
  S --> C: answer to the probe only,\nor connection closed
  C -> S: request in the clear\n(on a new connection if closed)
end
note over C, S: The peer is trusted for what SO_PEERCRED reports
@enduml
